<article class="env-theorem" id="0399">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0399">Theorem <span data-tag="0399">37.15.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism which is locally of finite presentation. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module which is locally of finite presentation. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  U = \{ x \in X \mid \mathcal{F}\text{ is flat over }S\text{ at }x\}   \]
</div>
  <p> is open in $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We may test for openness locally on $X$ hence we may assume that $f$ is a morphism of affine schemes. In this case the theorem is exactly Algebra, Theorem <a href="/tag/00RC" data-tag="00RC">10.129.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>